hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18153","Rawh narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi Husayn al-Makki narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever says, before he leaves and bends his leg from the Maghrib and dawn prayers: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner, His is the dominion and His is the praise, in His Hand is good, He gives life and causes death, and He has power over all things, ten times, there is written for him for each one ten good deeds, ten evil deeds are erased from him, ten degrees are raised for him, and they are a protection from every harm and a protection from the accursed Satan, and no sin may overtake him except association, and he will be among the best of people in deeds except a man who surpasses him by saying better than what he said."
"18154","Waki narrated to us, Abdul-Hamid narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Ghanm who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the brutish defamer, so he said: He is the strongly built, sound-bodied, big eater and drinker, who finds food and drink, oppressive to people, wide of belly."
"18155","Waki narrated to us, Abdul-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to me, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Ghanm who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A tribe of the Children of Israel perished, none knows where it perished, and I fear these lizards may be them."
"18156","Waki narrated to us, Abdul-Hamid narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Ghanm who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The coarse, the arrogant boaster, and the brutish defamer will not enter Paradise. He said: It fell from the book of my father."
"18157","Waki narrated to us, Abdul-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Ibn Ghanm al-Ashari, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: If you two agree in counsel, I will not oppose you."
"18158","Rawh narrated to us, Abdul-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, he said: I heard Shahr ibn Hawshab say: Abdur-Rahman ibn Ghanm narrated to me that al-Dari used to gift the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, every year a waterskin of wine. When the year it was prohibited came, he came with a waterskin. When the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, looked at him, he laughed and said: Have you not known that it has been prohibited after you? He said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not sell it and benefit from its price? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah cursed the Jews; they turned to what was prohibited to them of the fat of cattle and sheep, melted it, made it a price for themselves, and sold for what they eat. And wine is unlawful and its price is unlawful, and wine is unlawful and its price is unlawful, and wine is unlawful and its price is unlawful."
"18159","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abdul-Hamid narrated to us, he said: Shahr narrated to us, from Ibn Ghanm, that al-Dari used to gift the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned its meaning, except that he said: So they melted it and made it clarified fat, and sold for what they eat."
"18160","Abdussamad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Ghanm, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever adorns himself, or is adorned, with a glint of silk brocade with gold, will be branded with it on the Day of Resurrection."
"18161","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi al-Husayn, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Ghanm, conveying it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The best of the servants of Allah are those who, when seen, Allah is remembered; and the worst of the servants of Allah are those who go about with tale-bearing, dividing between loved ones, seeking hardship for the innocent."
